BenchLink (revision 3): a substitute finder for adult hockey leagues.
League admins import team rosters from a SportsEngine roster export (CSV),
captains see upcoming games and skater counts and request eligible subs from
other teams, both game captains approve each sub before contact details are
shared, and players keep their own phone number and sub availability current.
Revision 2 lets players list their preferred positions (C, LW, RW, D, G).
Revision 3 reads team divisions (Upper/Lower) and captain marks from a roster
CSV saved from Excel, and shows each viewer of a confirmed sub's contact card
only the other people.
BenchLink has no live SportsEngine connection and sends no SMS or email.

Built on the Fund2Build app kit v1 (src/appkit.py, copied verbatim). It uses
only the Python standard library and includes no third-party code or assets.
tests/sample_sportsengine_roster.txt and tests/sample_league_roster_upload.txt
contain fictional names and numbers.
